<title>LEBANON: Three-month T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Three-month T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields on Lebanese treasury bills were unchanged for the April 24 issue, except rates on three-month paper, which continued to decline, the Bank of Lebanon said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following rate details (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				 percent)		    (percent)</p>
<p>    24 month   (interest payable twice early)     16.08 (16.08)</p>
<p>    12 month		 13.20 (13.20)		15.20 (15.20)</p>
<p>The bank had announced on Monday yields for the shorter-term bills as follows:</p>
<p>    Six months	     13.48 (13.48)		14.45 (14.45)</p>
<p>    Three months	   13.25 (13.26)		13.70 (13.71)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
